 "intro": "Near Tribola in southern Spain, 147 BC. The Lusitanians, led by a former shepherd named Viriathus, have risen against Rome. You are the praetor Gaius Vetilius, who has trapped their army.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s account, the trapped Lusitanians offered to surrender, but Viriathus persuaded them to fight on. He drew them up for battle, then had them scatter while he held the Romans back with a thousand horsemen, and they met again at Tribola. Vetilius followed him into thickets, where he was ambushed; of 10,000 men, about 6,000 escaped. Vetilius was captured, and killed by a soldier who did not know who he was. Viriathus fought Rome for eight more years. The other choices are what-ifs.",
